# PLAN-915 R02/R03 scenario suite — the two ns=scenario AV cells the plan
# owns (binding.tsv:113-114), NOT the same-named corpus rows R02/R03.
#
# R02 (构造/clone/扩容失败注入): the frozen corpus programs L04/L05/V05/LSTR/K02
# are driven through the real frontends and the recipe sweeps EVERY
# allocation attempt on both existing seams (value allocations: slot
# writes, closure-env materialization, list capacity growth; owned arena:
# Str/List buffers), then asserts the N+1 positive control and a real re-run
# after the fault is cleared. Sources are byte-copies of the corpus
# `src/<ID>.at` files; the parent freezes the result value and both attempt
# counts in its own table (never the worker's word). A typed capture-clone
# control covers the prepare-level clone path the source subset cannot mint
# (a borrow-capturing closure may not escape).
#
# R03 (活借用/旧 buffer): AutoLang source cannot mint a List Place, so the
# runtime witness is a typed MIR module that passes the same verifier gates
# (`verify_mir` → `encode_abc` → `verify_abc_bytes`) and runs on the real
# executor: mint a place, read it legally, mutate the list structurally
# (push/insert/remove/element replace), then use the OLD place — it must
# trap `av.trap.stale-place` BEFORE any buffer access (the gated counters
# report buffer_reads=1: the legal read only). Fresh-token and no-mutation
# controls keep every legal neighbour usable, and a source-level
# counterexample shows the STATIC rejection of a structural mutation while
# iterating (the two faces stay distinct).

```test-case
case {
  schema: "autolang.case/2"
  id: "ace.m1.r02.l04"
  tags: ["ace-m1", "scenario", "resource-915", "r02"]
  links: ["PLAN-915"]
  source: { file: "src/L04-915.at", syntax: "auto", path: "main.at" }
  entry: { mode: "program" }
  checks: [
    { id: "av-r02-l04-sweep", adapter: "probe", action: "run",
      options: { recipe: "ac-av/resource-run-v1", av: { entry: "source:l04" }, steps: [ { op: "run" } ] },
      expect: { completion: "success" } }
  ]
}
```

